"""Retain the designated QuPath project and coordinate its permitted changes.

The runtime records stable project identity, current image entries, registered script
operations and project-write completion. A writer lease binds each operation to the expected
project and current saved state. Native results must match their selected image and
requested operation before their completion is published.

Live image-catalogue checks compare scientific content rather than routine viewing metadata.
Historical stage records retain the exact snapshots and results they consumed. Project
creation, classifier publication and accepted annotation updates therefore share one
controlled write history."""

